  "body": "## What\n\nRecord the five native binary provider probes, versioned source commits, and a provisional Tempo pin. Ignore clone-local `.observability/` state. This is the independent provider research slice of #110.\n\n## Why\n\nThe current Tempo 3.0.3 release has no macOS asset, while the 2.7.2 release has a native arm64 binary. Grafana 13.2.2 also needs its publisher archive because its GitHub release has no macOS asset. The lifecycle, configuration, and profiling work exceeds the 800-unit issue limit when sized with tests and docs. Issue #107 has not activated the notebook commands required for profiling.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Harness: Codex CLI 0.157.1. Model: `gpt-6-sol` at high effort.\n- [Provider matrix](https://github.com/tbhb/agent-orchestration-poc/blob/research/110-observability-stack/research/gates/observability/provider-matrix.csv) records five successful mise installation and version probes on macOS arm64.\n- [Research notes](https://github.com/tbhb/agent-orchestration-poc/blob/research/110-observability-stack/research/gates/observability/notes.md) record the two failed current-release provider probes, exact commands, and the provisional Tempo choice.\n- [Source versions](https://github.com/tbhb/agent-orchestration-poc/blob/research/110-observability-stack/research/gates/observability/versions.md) identify the six upstream commits and versioned material read.\n- `mise run check` and `mise run check:mutation` concluded success after merging current `main`. `mise run build` and `mise run docs:build` concluded success. The five-row CSV validation and the staged secret scan passed.\n- `mise run docs:check-links` exited 1 locally because Chromium closed at launch and the validator then reported five links in unchanged pages. No site page changes are in this PR.\n\n## Docs\n\nThe version and provider research is committed. The observability design, runbook, decision, experiment notebook, claims, and reviewer artifacts remain in the dependent lifecycle and verified-profile slices.\n\n## Size justification\n\nThis PR is 60 added nonblank units and no code lines against `main`, below the 400-unit target. A revised estimate for all #110 criteria is about 1,050 units. The coordinator needs dependent lifecycle and ingestion, then verified-profile work items with reserved paths. The latter waits for runnable #107. The current PR does not claim a running stack or completed #110 acceptance.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [ ] CI green after this PR's checks conclude.\n- [x] Docs impact recorded in the open issue and split proposal.\n- [x] No secrets in committed evidence.\n- [x] Provider evidence committed.\n\nRefs: #110\n",
